{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision the local designer, reviewer, and visitor accounts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three local accounts were created, remained present after reboot, and were locked against password login.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a69d2d1fa74a42e7","cmd-9cd577cb661b487b","cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide inherited access under the projects directory so new designer-created directories and documents are readable and writable by reviewer, inaccessible to visitor, and remain owned by designer without periodic permission repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Default POSIX ACLs were installed throughout the directory chain. Designer-created nested directories and files inherited reviewer access and explicit visitor denial despite umask 077; reviewer directly read and modified the document, visitor operations were denied, and ownership remained designer. A new file created after reboot demonstrated persistent inheritance. The command trace shows an ACL-based implementation rather than a periodic repair process.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a69d2d1fa74a42e7","cmd-483d963af7da4ae6","cmd-9cd577cb661b487b","cmd-6dcb908bf9e34871","cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the existing project contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The only baseline file beneath projects, brief.txt, retained its original SHA-256 digest before configuration, after configuration, and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-d0d9def0e7314a4a","cmd-9cd577cb661b487b","cmd-6dcb908bf9e34871","cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged after execution and reboot; the solution used the platform's installed POSIX ACL tooling.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0d9def0e7314a4a","cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account creation and ACL changes were required implementation actions (cmd-a69d2d1fa74a42e7); the retained handoff-verification files and reviewer append were bounded functional evidence (cmd-483d963af7da4ae6, cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5); and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-db01a57735f64629). The initial unprivileged useradd attempt stopped at the first permission error with no evidence of state change (cmd-8219dc84a1f44932). Temporary probe files were absent after reboot, package health remained clean, and no services were failed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8219dc84a1f44932","cmd-a69d2d1fa74a42e7","cmd-483d963af7da4ae6","cmd-db01a57735f64629","cmd-365c09f0d14d4eb5","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, changed boot identity, and recovered its system, SSH service, accounts, data, ACL inheritance, ownership, and access behavior. The lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The explicit scheduled-job search covered conventional cron locations but did not enumerate systemd timers. However, the complete executor timeline contains no command creating any periodic job, and direct creation tests demonstrate default-ACL inheritance.","No separate cluster-state probe was applicable to this single-node, non-clustered task; recovered system and service state were directly observed."]}
